-- **Travel pattern:** A solitary field season, then home to write it up; she flies her own routes with no timetable, and long trips only for a relic rumour or another pony's crisis.
-- **Era variants:** At the end of canon she is a semi-retired legend who still answers the right rumour. The EQG film-world A.K. Yearling is a different-world writer whose props were approved for a movie; IDW's 'Bravely Blue' alternate and the Pony Life cameo are labelled and not merged with this card. She has no G5 appearance.
-- **Uncertainty:** The cottage sits north-west near Vanhoover and the Galloping Gorge, but her adventure turf — the Tenochtitlan Basin, Somnambula and 'Southern Equestria' — is desert south, and the infobox joins two regions that do not obviously meet. Both place names are map/tie-in only and never on-screen settings, so the bearing is map-derived (Medium) and the distance unquantifiable (Low). The chapter-book Pranceton degree, the Canterlot archive post, the uncle and the beach walks are secondary canon.
